        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\n> Hence, plugins which support both `mini.icons` and `nvim-web-devicons` might unintentionally use `mini.icons` instead. This is the behaviour of `snacks.nvim` as can be seen from this [snippet](https://github.com/folke/snacks.nvim/blob/bc0630e43be5699bb94dadc302c0d21615421d93/lua/snacks/util/init.lua#L125-L154) from its codebase, where it checks for `mini.icon` first before checking for `nvim-web-devicons`.\n\nThe code snippet doesn't follow [recommended suggestion](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/7bbafa4691147bc8b74a51986b957daca14c1876/doc/mini-icons.txt#L38-L39) on how to do this, which is explicitly takes into account the use case described here (there is 'mini.icons' present but user doesn't want to use it in favor of 'nvim-web-devicons'). So my suggestion is either to adjust the code in 'snacks.nvim' or start using 'mini.icons' :)",
